.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_CHANGE_IDENTITY 3 2026-11-06 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_change_identity \- change one exact staged locale/platform identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_change_identity("
.BI "        mpq_update_s *" "update,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "locale,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "platform,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "new_locale,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "new_platform"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects exactly the stored filename, locale and platform in the current
successful transaction stage and changes its locale/platform tuple. There is
no implicit neutral fallback or global locale state. An identical tuple
validates the exact source and succeeds without changing the working file.
.PP
Classic-only v1-v4 archives support shared-block aliases and unrelated
unknown-name members. Hash A/B and the selected probe slot are preserved.
Only the selected tuple changes; all other ordinary identities retain their
association with the original payload. Canonical member numbers may remap
when metadata is rebuilt, as for other transactional operations.
.PP
Ordinary member offsets, packed bytes, storage flags, attributes and timestamps
are preserved. Payloads are neither detached nor re-encoded. A tuple change
requires no encryption or FIX_KEY transformation because it changes neither
the basename nor the physical member offset. Source raw-chunk policy is
retained, and applicable raw and structural digests are regenerated. An
unchanged listfile is also preserved unless signature invalidation requires
removing its signature entry.
.PP
Mixed classic/HET/BET targets require consistent one-to-one mappings and full
extended hashes. Shared BET rows, ambiguous provenance and unsupported metadata
are rejected. HET/BET-only entries cannot acquire classic locale/platform
selectors; their only supported operation is an unchanged unqualified tuple.
Special-member qualifier mutations are rejected, but valid identical-tuple
requests remain no-ops. Existing reconstruction limits, including embedded
wrappers and unrelated trailers, apply to actual changes.
.PP
The operation borrows filename only for this synchronous call. A rejected
operation preserves the previous valid transaction stage and original source.
Commit publishes only finalized output. Modifications follow the existing
signature-invalidation policy. Transactions containing only no-op requests
preserve the original bytes.
Commit and abort consume the transaction, including on error.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST reports a missing source identity, an occupied destination
identity or an invalid required argument. LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT reports
ambiguous, contradictory or unrepresentable metadata. Allocation, size and I/O
failures use the existing LIBMPQ_ERROR_* values. No rejected operation publishes
partially rebuilt output.
